πFish

Minimal X11 window manager in C. Ratpoison-inspired frames, Emacs-inspired keys

Keys

Press C-t, release it, then press a key below

Key          Action
2 / 3        Split top/bottom / side by side
0 / 1        Delete frame / keep only this frame
C-f / C-b    Next / previous frame
C-n / C-p    Next / previous window
w / b        List windows / select by number
! / k        Run program / close window
x            Command prompt
?            Active keybindings
q / r        Quit / restart

C-g or Escape cancels a sequence or prompt

Commands

Open with C-t x, type a command

exec xterm
select 2
split-vertical
reload-config

Backspace deletes a character. C-u clears the prompt

Configuration

Edit ~/.fishrc. Defaults work without this file

prefix C-t
bind Tab next-frame
bind n next-window
bind p previous-window
bind Return exec xterm
bind R reload-config

exec feh --no-fehbg --bg-fill "$HOME/Pictures/wallpaper.jpg"
